[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/dtn の gossip ベース peer discovery（kotoba.dtn.discovery）の設計根拠" "このADRシリーズ（2607161743〜）の完了宣言と最終到達点の記録"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161922-kotoba-lang-dtn-multi-hop-relay-routing.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161956-kotoba-lang-bytes-shared-primitives-extraction.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162020-kotoba-lang-turn-allocation-state-machine.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "adr-2607162202-kotoba-lang-dtn-gossip-peer-discovery", :adr/doc_type :adr, :adr/last_verified "2026-07-16", :adr/body "---\nid: adr-2607162202-kotoba-lang-dtn-gossip-peer-discovery\ntitle: \"ADR-2607162202: kotoba-lang/dtn gains gossip-based peer discovery via kotoba-lang/io-libp2p (Phase 5) — closing the independent telecom substrate's originating gap\"\nstatus: accepted\ndoc_type: adr\ntopic: telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite\nauthoritative: true\nlast_verified: 2026-07-16\nauthoritative_for:\n  - kotoba-lang/dtn の gossip ベース peer discovery（kotoba.dtn.discovery）の設計根拠\n  - このADRシリーズ（2607161743〜）の完了宣言と最終到達点の記録\nrelated:\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161922-kotoba-lang-dtn-multi-hop-relay-routing.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161956-kotoba-lang-bytes-shared-primitives-extraction.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162020-kotoba-lang-turn-allocation-state-machine.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport.edn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\nsupersedes: []\nsuperseded_by: []\n---\n\n# ADR-2607162202: kotoba-lang/dtn gains gossip-based peer discovery via kotoba-lang/io-libp2p (Phase 5) — closing the independent telecom substrate's originating gap\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Problem\n\nEvery ADR in this series since ADR-2607161743 named the same limitation\nrepeatedly: `kotoba-lang/dtn`'s internet-overlay transport requires a\npeer's host:port to already be known — no discovery. ADR-2607161743's\nDecision 4 named `kotoba-lang/net` (gossip) as the intended future\ncomposition point for this; ADR-2607162033's own Consequences explicitly\ndeferred it as \"Phase 5, not yet started.\" This ADR is that phase, and the\nlast of this consolidation plan: `kotoba-lang/dtn` nodes now announce\ntheir own reachability and consume announcements over a real\n`kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` gossip mesh (Phase 4, ADR-2607162135), so two\n`dtn` nodes that were never told about each other in advance can still\ndiscover one another and exchange a real message.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: `kotoba.dtn.discovery` — a direct, real dependency on `io-libp2p`, unlike `dtn`'s deliberate non-dependency on `rcs`\n\n`kotoba-lang/dtn`'s `deps.edn` gains `io.github.kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\n{:local/root \"../io-libp2p\"}`. This is a genuine, structural dependency —\nunlike `kotoba.dtn.gateway`'s deliberate duck-typed decoupling from\n`kotoba-lang/rcs` (ADR-2607161743 Decision 2, chosen because the two\nlibraries were built in parallel and needed to stay build-order\nindependent), `io-libp2p` already existed, stable and tested, by the time\nthis phase began; there was no parallel-build reason to avoid a direct\ndependency here, and a direct dependency is simpler and more honest about\nwhat `kotoba.dtn.discovery` actually requires to function.\n\n- `announce!`/`start-announcing!` — publish a `dtn`-node's own reachability\n  (`:dtn/e164`/`:dtn/host`/`:dtn/port`/`:dtn/transport-kind`) as a gossip\n  message on a well-known topic, periodically.\n- `process-presence-updates!`/`start-discovering!` — poll the gossip\n  node's existing `:received-messages` observable state (an external,\n  read-only consumer — `io-libp2p` itself was not modified) for new\n  presence announcements, translate each into a `dtn` peer-table entry,\n  merge it into a **running** `dtn` node's `:peers` map, and explicitly\n  filter out self-announcements.\n- The pure translation/validation/self-detection/dedup-index logic lives\n  in `kotoba.dtn.discovery.presence` (`.cljc`), gaining 28 new\n  `clojure.test` assertions — the impure polling/scheduling wiring lives in\n  `kotoba.dtn.discovery` (`.cljs`), matching this whole series' consistent\n  \"pure decision, impure I/O, in separate namespaces\" discipline.\n\n### Decision 2: this is gossip-based presence broadcast, explicitly not a DHT, and explicitly not authenticated at the announcement layer\n\nStated plainly in the namespace docstring and README: no distributed hash\ntable, no structured routing overlay — every node in the gossip mesh sees\nevery presence announcement via `io-libp2p`'s existing fanout, and a\npresence announcement is trusted at face value (an attacker on the gossip\nmesh could announce a false E.164→address mapping). Combining discovered\npeers with `kotoba.dtn.auth`'s `:peer-secrets` for the actual bundle\ntraffic once a peer is discovered is the caller's responsibility — this\nmodule does not do it automatically, and does not claim to. Discovery is\npolling-based (periodic `js/setInterval` scans of observable state) rather\nthan push/callback-based, a deliberate simplicity choice given\n`io-libp2p`'s current integration surface — recorded as the reason\n`io-libp2p` itself needed no modification, not as an oversight.\n\n### Decision 3: a real gossip-dedup interaction was found and fixed on the `dtn` side, without touching `io-libp2p`\n\n`kotoba.net.gossip/route-message` dedups by content-hash, and a `publish!`\ncall marks its own payload seen on the sender's own seen-cache\nimmediately. A periodic re-announcement with unchanged fields hashes\nidentically every tick — after the first successful broadcast, every\nfollowing one would have silently become a no-op, which would have broken\nexactly the late-joiner scenario (Scenario 3): a peer joining after the\nfirst (and only effectively-delivered) broadcast would never receive one\nat all. Fixed entirely within `kotoba-lang/dtn`: `presence-announcement`\nnow stamps a real `js/Date.now()` `:dtn/announce-ts`, making every tick's\npayload content-distinct and forcing a genuine re-fanout attempt each\ninterval. This is the same category of finding as `io-libp2p`'s own\n`safe-from` workaround for the `#{from self}` duplicate-key issue\n(ADR-2607162135 Decision 2) — an interaction between a caller's usage\npattern and `gossip.cljc`'s existing dedup semantics, designed around\nrather than requiring a change to the pure library itself.\n\n### Decision 4: three scenarios, the third deliberately testing the harder, less obvious direction\n\nScenario 1 proves the headline claim: node A's `:peers` map is observed\ngenuinely empty immediately after `start-node!`, then populated by\ndiscovery alone, then a real `send-message!` to a never-statically-configured\npeer succeeds and is received. Scenario 2 proves self-filtering — and,\nworth recording as a specific rigor practice, the implementing agent\nexplicitly flagged that a full-mesh gossip topology alone would make this\nproof *vacuous* (since `gossip.cljc`'s own transport-layer `{from self}`\nexclusion already prevents a node's own broadcast from round-tripping back\nto it in a full mesh, regardless of whether `kotoba.dtn.discovery`'s own\nself-filtering code does anything at all), and added a second, genuinely\nnon-vacuous check: directly crafting and injecting a self-announcement\ninto a node's own observed gossip state, proving THIS module's filtering\nlogic — not just topology — is what keeps a node's own address out of its\nown peer table. Scenario 3 proves discovery is symmetric (a late-joining\nnode discovers pre-existing peers, not only the reverse) — the harder,\nless obvious direction to get right, deliberately tested rather than\nassumed from Scenario 1's happy path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `dtn`'s `clojure -M:test` → 35 tests / 175 assertions (was 147; +28 new for `kotoba.dtn.discovery.presence`), 0 failures, 0 errors. Independently re-run from a cold clone.\n- `dtn`'s `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings. Independently re-run.\n- `dtn`'s pre-existing 7-scenario transport demo (`test/kotoba/dtn/transport/tcp_demo.cljs`) → still `RESULT: 7/7 scenarios passed`, exit 0, unmodified. Independently re-run from a cold clone.\n- `nbb --classpath \"src:test:../phone/src:../html/src:../css/src:../wire/src:../bytes/src:../io-libp2p/src\" test/kotoba/dtn/discovery_demo.cljs` → `RESULT: 3/3 scenarios passed`, exit 0. Independently re-run from a cold clone by the orchestrating session — output identical to the implementing agent's report, including every intermediate `:peers` map snapshot and gossip-recv log line.\n- `kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` confirmed untouched (`git status --short` empty after cloning fresh and checking) — this ADR's real dependency (Decision 1) did not require modifying its provider.\n- Pushed to `github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn` (public), commit `679a5ed5daef1780e38c29cd6f2181aadb9f727f`.\n- `manifest/west.yml`: pin advanced via `--entry dtn` (1-line diff, `b55090713aaf→679a5ed5daef`, `verify-west-pins: 1 件の pin 変更をすべて検証 OK`), landed via an isolated sibling-path worktree + GitHub API server-side merge, matching every prior ADR in this series.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The originating gap this entire ADR series exists to close — *「今の\n  kotoba-lang, cloud-itonami に既存の電話通信網、sms, rcs に依存しない独自かつ\n  全く同じ規格の telecom 基盤は設計されている?」* (ADR-2607161743) followed by\n  *「gap を埋めて、実際に稼働可能な前提に」* — is now closed for the\n  internet-overlay leg end-to-end: real transport (ADR-2607161817), real\n  resilience (ADR-2607161852), real multi-hop relay (ADR-2607161922), real\n  security (ADR-2607161951), and now real discovery (this ADR) compose into\n  a substrate where two nodes with zero prior static configuration of each\n  other can find one another and exchange an authenticated,\n  replay-protected, SMS/RCS-wire-compatible message.\n- The shared-library consolidation side-goal (owner directive: \"net, turn\n  をちゃんと実装, 共有libを設計して効率化, 依存効率化\") is also complete: two\n  independent, real network services (`dtn`'s DTN substrate,\n  `org-ietf-turn`'s relay) share `kotoba-lang/bytes` and\n  `kotoba-lang/wire`'s foundations, and `dtn` now also directly composes\n  with `io-libp2p` for discovery — three genuine cross-repo dependency\n  relationships proving the efficiency goal, not just extracted-but-unused\n  libraries.\n- Still explicitly undone, honestly inventoried across this whole series\n  and not newly closed here: NAT traversal via `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn`\n  (deliberately out of this ADR's scope — TURN is UDP, `dtn`'s transport is\n  TCP, bridging them is a materially different problem, named as a\n  possible future Phase 6, not attempted); mesh-radio/satellite hardware\n  (environment-blocked, not code-blocked); real carrier SMS/RCS gateway\n  credentials; a consuming cloud-itonami actor; PKI/full replay-window\n  hardening beyond what ADR-2607161951 already closed; `gossip.cljc`'s own\n  `#{from self}` bug (found in ADR-2607162135, still only worked around,\n  not fixed at the source); multi-hop relay chains beyond two hops\n  (verified only for the two-hop case, per ADR-2607161922's own honest\n  scoping).\n- Discovery's trust model (Decision 2) means a production deployment of\n  this substrate would need to layer authentication onto the discovery\n  channel itself, not just the subsequent bundle traffic — named here as a\n  real, disclosed limitation for anyone building on this work, not silently\n  assumed away.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **A DHT-based discovery mechanism** instead of flat gossip broadcast.\n  Rejected: `io-libp2p`'s existing real capability is gossip fanout, not a\n  DHT; building DHT machinery from scratch to enable discovery would have\n  been a materially larger, separate undertaking disproportionate to what\n  \"close the discovery gap\" actually required.\n- **Authenticating presence announcements themselves** (e.g. requiring a\n  signature over the announcement payload) as part of this phase.\n  Rejected for this pass — recorded as a real, disclosed gap (Decision 2's\n  Consequences) rather than silently scoped in; combining discovery with\n  `kotoba.dtn.auth`'s existing HMAC mechanism for the announcement channel\n  itself is legitimate, separable future work.\n- **Fixing `kotoba.net.gossip`'s dedup-by-content-hash behavior directly**\n  to accommodate periodic unchanged-payload re-broadcasts as a first-class\n  case, instead of working around it with a timestamp field on the `dtn`\n  side. Rejected for the same reason `io-libp2p` itself wasn't modified for\n  the `#{from self}` issue: this task's scope was `dtn`-side integration,\n  not `io-libp2p` library changes; the workaround is complete, honest, and\n  narrower in blast radius than changing shared dedup semantics that other\n  gossip consumers also rely on.\n- **Attempting NAT traversal via `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` in the same\n  phase**, since it was the other half of the \"元々のgap\" alongside\n  discovery. Rejected: TURN's UDP relay and `dtn`'s TCP transport don't\n  compose without a materially different bridging design (a UDP-tunneled\n  TCP variant, or a UDP-native `dtn` transport) — attempting both in one\n  phase risked doing neither well; discovery alone is a complete, coherent,\n  independently valuable unit of work.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn` (originating problem statement)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161922-kotoba-lang-dtn-multi-hop-relay-routing.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161956-kotoba-lang-bytes-shared-primitives-extraction.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162020-kotoba-lang-turn-allocation-state-machine.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport.edn`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/discovery.cljs`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/discovery/presence.cljc`\n", :adr/artifacts "{:kotoba-lang-dtn \"kotoba-lang/dtn @ 679a5ed5daef (pushed, public)\", :manifest \"orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn pin advanced via --entry dtn, pin-verified\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607162202: kotoba-lang/dtn gains gossip-based peer discovery via kotoba-lang/io-libp2p (Phase 5) — closing the independent telecom substrate's originating gap", :adr/source-format "edn"}]